  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Always include the opposite ending on the same base, such as full of hope beside without hope.",
      "The other two wrong taps must be true meanings of different allowed -ful or -less words, never nonsense phrases.",
      "Never offer the bare base alone as a choice. Help is not the meaning of helpful.",
      "Keep about half the pool -ful and half -less. Kid world only: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather.",
      "Tier 1 uses far bases such as help, hope, and care. Tier 3 uses near bases such as help and hope, or care and use.",
      "Do not name the ending in the stem. Show the word or a short kid sentence. No real names. Use <NAME>.",
      "When the stem has a concrete noun, add one lemma_lookup picture for that noun. Never invent audio files."
    ]
  },
